{"id":"u-5eb3745c-6bc3-4b5f-a0bc-6103a1da70e5","src":"community","title":"Iron & Ultra: Dip Strenght + Ultra running","author":"William Borsand","url":"https://www.boostcamp.app/users/3ibnEq-untitled-program","desc":"Iron & Ultra is a 6-week hybrid program for athletes who want to build a bigger dip 1RM without giving up the miles that ultra running demands. Instead of treating strength and endurance as competing goals, it organizes the week so each supports the other.\n\nUpper-body training is built around four sessions a week: two heavy days where you work up to top sets on the dip and back off for volume, and two technique days with paused reps and lower-fatigue work (RIR 3). Around the dip you’ll train pulling, overhead pressing, arms, and calisthenics skill work, so shoulders and elbows stay healthy under frequent loading. There are no dedicated leg days, which leaves your legs fresh for running.\n\nRunning fills the days between lifting. Expect easy aerobic runs, one quality session, and a weekly long run of 90 to 120 minutes, with short, easy runs optional on lifting days. Hard sessions stay hard and easy sessions stay easy, so you can recover well enough to progress in both.\nPrefer bench? Swap the dip for the bench press in any session, with the same sets, reps, and intensities.\nWho it’s for: Athletes who already lift and run regularly, want a stronger dip, and are training for ultra-distance races.","level":["Advanced","Intermediate"],"goals":["Athletics","Muscle","Strength"],"equipment":["Full Gym"],"minutes":50,"joins":0,"rate":0,"rateCount":0,"updated":"2026-10-10T12:52:26.702Z","variations":[{"name":"default","days":["Hard day","Zone 1 / Threshold","Easy","Zone 1","Hard","Easy","Long run"],"weeks":[[{"ex":[{"n":"Run","sets":[{"sec":1200}]},{"n":"Dip (Weighted)","sets":[{"lo":3,"hi":6,"rpe":9.5},{"lo":8,"hi":20,"rpe":9.5}]},{"n":"Pull-Up (Weighted)","sets":[{"lo":6,"hi":10,"rpe":8.5}]},{"n":"Pull-Up (Bodyweight)","sets":[{"amrap":1,"rpe":8.5}]},{"n":"T